Send the page referrer on adaptive-streaming child requests.

Native HLS: the master playlist is fetched by the pipeline's main
WebKitWebSrc with the player's referrer, but variant playlists and media
segments are fetched by child sources created inside the adaptive demuxer.
Those children (a) never receive the player referrer (sourceSetup only fires
for the main source) and (b) get Referer=<playlist URI> stamped by the
demuxer via the extra-headers property, which is applied AFTER
setHTTPReferrer and overrides it. CDNs that validate the page referer reject
the result — device-proven on pornhub's phncdn HLS segments: 404 with the
playlist referer (no ACAO on the error → CORS failure →
MEDIA_ERR_SRC_NOT_SUPPORTED), 200 with the page referer and a browser UA.

Three legs, all gated by WEBKIT_GST_NO_SOUP_REFERER=1 (unset = fix active):
- configureElement hands every WebKitWebSrc (element-setup is deep, so this
  reaches demuxer children) the player's referrer.
- webKitWebSrcMakeRequest re-asserts that referrer after extra-headers.
- souphttpsrc elements (not used by this port's demuxer, but harmless) get
  the referrer via their own extra-headers.

--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer.cpp
@@ -2732,6 +2732,30 @@
     if (gst_check_version(1, 22, 0) && startsWith(name.span(), "urisourcebin"_s) && (isBlob || isMediaSource() || isMediaStreamPlayer()))
         g_object_set(element, "use-buffering", FALSE, "parse-streams", !isMediaStreamPlayer(), nullptr);
 
+    // HLS/DASH child fetches (variant playlists, media segments) are done by
+    // souphttpsrc elements the adaptive demuxer creates internally, bypassing
+    // WebKitWebSrc — so they carry no Referer. Some CDNs validate it
+    // (device-proven on pornhub's *-h.phncdn.com edges: HTTP 412 without a
+    // Referer, 200 with one), which kills native HLS playback right after the
+    // master manifest. Forward the player's referrer to every souphttpsrc.
+    // WEBKIT_GST_NO_SOUP_REFERER=1 restores upstream behavior.
+    if (startsWith(name.span(), "souphttpsrc"_s) && !m_referrer.isEmpty()
+        && !g_getenv("WEBKIT_GST_NO_SOUP_REFERER")) {
+        GUniquePtr<GstStructure> headers(gst_structure_new("extra-headers",
+            "Referer", G_TYPE_STRING, m_referrer.utf8().data(), nullptr));
+        g_object_set(element, "extra-headers", headers.get(), nullptr);
+    }
+
+    // Same problem on the WebKitWebSrc path (which is what the adaptive
+    // demuxer actually uses in this port): child sources for variant
+    // playlists / segments never see sourceSetup, so their referrer stays
+    // empty and the demuxer's extra-headers Referer=<playlist URI> is what
+    // goes on the wire. Hand every WebKitWebSrc the player's referrer;
+    // webKitWebSrcMakeRequest re-asserts it over extra-headers.
+    if (WEBKIT_IS_WEB_SRC(element) && !m_referrer.isEmpty()
+        && !g_getenv("WEBKIT_GST_NO_SOUP_REFERER"))
+        webKitWebSrcSetReferrer(WEBKIT_WEB_SRC_CAST(element), m_referrer);
+
     if (startsWith(name.span(), "parsebin"_s))
         configureParsebin(element);
 
--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/WebKitWebSourceGStreamer.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/WebKitWebSourceGStreamer.cpp
@@ -691,6 +691,16 @@
         });
     }
 
+    // Re-assert the player's referrer over the demuxer-provided extra-headers:
+    // the adaptive demuxer stamps Referer=<playlist URI> on its child sources,
+    // and CDNs that validate the page referer reject those requests
+    // (device-proven on phncdn HLS segments: 404 with the playlist referer,
+    // 200 with the page referer). members->referrer is the page referrer,
+    // pushed to every WebKitWebSrc by MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer's
+    // element-setup handler. WEBKIT_GST_NO_SOUP_REFERER=1 disables.
+    if (!members->referrer.isEmpty() && !g_getenv("WEBKIT_GST_NO_SOUP_REFERER"))
+        request.setHTTPReferrer(members->referrer);
+
     // We always request Icecast/Shoutcast metadata, just in case ...
     request.setHTTPHeaderField(HTTPHeaderName::IcyMetadata, "1"_s);
 
